Hello everyone,

I have an new issue with the bass speakers of my Lenovo Yoga 7i (16", 
7). It has the "00:1f.3 Multimedia audio controller: Intel Corporation 
Alder Lake PCH-P High Definition Audio Controller (rev 01)."
On Kernel Version 6.6.63-1 it was possible to get the bass speakers 
working by passing the "options snd-sof-intel-hda-common 
hda_model=alc287-yoga9-bass-spk-pin" Kernel module parameter. Without 
it, only the tremble speakers are utilized, causing bad audio quality.
On Kernel Version 6.11.10-2 this fix does not work anymore.

I'm sorry but i am not knowledgeable enough to further diagnose the problem.

